$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A solution of TiCl4 in CH2Cl2 (1 M, 2.8 ml, 2.8 mmol) was added to a
solution of the obtained aldol (530 mg, 2.34 mmol) stirred at -78°C in
anhydrous CH2Cl2 (5 ml) . The mixture was stirred at -78°C for 10 min.
BH3-Py complex (0.7 ml, 7 mmol) was added dropwise, and stirring was
continued for 2 h. The cold mixture was quenched by addition of aqueous
HCl (1 M) and extracted with CH2Cl2. The combined organic phases were
washed with brine and concentrated. The residue was dissolved in
MeOH-Et2O (1:1) and treated with aqueous NaOH (3 N) and 30% H2O2
overnight. The resulting mixture was extracted with EtOAc, washed with
brine, dried with MgSO4, and concentrated. Preparative column
chromatography on silica gel (hexane-EtOAc 3:2 as eluent) afforded
meso-1,3-diphenylpropane-1,3-diol 28. White solid, yield 0.34 g (1.5
mmol, 64%). 1H NMR (400.13 MHz, CDCl3), δ, ppm (J, Hz): 7.39-7.31 (8H, m,
arom.); 7.28-7.26 (2H, m, arom.); 4.98 (2H, dd, J = 10.1, J = 2.8,
PhCHOH); 3.71 (2H, br. s, OH); 2.17 (1H, dt, J = 14.6, J = 10.1, СН2);
1.95 (1H, dt, J = 14.6, J = 2.8, СН2). 13C NMR (100.65 MHz, CDCl3), δ,
ppm: 144.1 (2C); 128.4 (+, 4C); 127.6 (+, 2C); 125.7 (+, 4C); 74.9 (+,
2C); 47.6 (-).
