$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Reduction of α-Keto Aldoxime O-Ethers with
Borane/Oxazaborolidine; General Procedure : To a solution of the
appropriate amino alcohol (2 mmol) in THF (10 mL) was added 10 M BMS
(borane-methyl sulfide complex) (0.2 mL, 2 mmol) and the mixture was
stirred at r.t. for 1 h. THF (5 mL) and the rest of BMS (0.8 mL, 8 mmol)
were added and the mixture was stirred for another 10 min. The mixture
was cooled to 0 °C and α-keto aldoxime ether (2 mmol) in THF (15 mL) was
added in 2.5 h using a syringe pump. The mixture was stirred at 0 °C for
10 min, at r.t. for 30 min, and refluxed for 18 h. After cooling to r.t.,
aq 3 M HCl (12 mL) was added slowly and the mixture was allowed to stir
for 5 h. THF was removed on a rotary evaporator; then EtOAc (30 mL) and
NaCl (5 g) were added to the residue, and the mixture was basified with
aq 10% NaOH to pH 12 and stirred for 5 min. The organic layer was
separated and the residue was extracted with EtOAc (5 x 15 mL). The
combined organic extracts were dried (MgSO4). The solvent was removed and
the product was isolated by flash chromatography on silica gel
(CH2Cl2-MeOH, 90:10). The product was derivatized with trifluoroacetic
anhydride in the presence of Et3N and analyzed by GC on a chiral β-Dex
325 capillary column (30 m x 0.25 mm). Commercially available chiral
2-amino-1-phenylethanols were also derivatized with trifluoroacetic
anhydride and analyzed by GC as comparative samples.
(R)-2-Amino-1-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethanol (29) as a colorless oil, yield
49%, 77% ee. GC: tR = 50.49 (R), tR = 53.31 (S), T = 160 °C, f = 35
mL/min. 1H NMR (700 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 2.86 (br s, 1 H, CH2, part of ABX
system), 3.01 (br s, 1 H, CH2, part of ABX system), 3.48 (br s, 3 H, OH,
NH2), 3.79 (s, 3 H, CH3), 4.70 (br s, 1 H, CH, part of ABX system), 6.80
(dd, J = 8.4, 2.1 Hz 1 H, CHarom), 6.90 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1 H, CHarom),
6.92 (d, J = 2.1 Hz, 1 H, CHarom), 7.24 (dd, J = 8.4, 7.7 Hz, 1 H,
CHarom). 13C NMR (175 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 48.87 (CH2), 55.19 (CH3), 77.20
(CH), 111.35 (CHarom), 113.00 (CHarom), 118.14 (CHarom), 129.42 (CHarom),
144.07 (Carom), 159.71 (Carom). Anal. Calcd for C9H13NO2: C, 64.65; H,
7.84; N, 8.38. Found: C, 64.58; H, 7.83; N, 8.30.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, incremental addition of reagent in stage 1 substage 1,
