$DATUM (S)-2-Hydroxy-2-phenylacetaldehyde O-Methyl Oxime (S)-26 by Transfer
Hydrogenation: To a mixture of 5 (0.163 g, 1 mmol), EtOAc (4 mL), and an
azeotropic mixture of formic acid-Et3N (5:2, 0.2 mL) was added
RhCl[(R,R)-TsDPEN](C5Me5) (5 mg) and the mixture stirred at r.t. for 24
h. The solvents were removed and the product was isolated by flash
chromatography on silica gel (n-hexane-EtOAc-CH2Cl2-MeOH, 6:0.5:0.5:0.5).
Colorless oil, yield 0.074 g, 45%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 2.05 (br
s, 1 H, OH), 3.89 (s, 3 H, CH3), 5.33 (d, J = 5.0 Hz, 1 H, CH), 7.31-7.41
(m, 5 H, CHarom), 7.47 (d, J = 5.0 Hz, 1 H, CH). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3):
δ = 61.90 (CH3), 71.65 (CH), 126.36 (2 CHarom), 128.25 (CHarom), 128.74
(2 CHarom), 139.65 (Carom), 150.21 (CH). Anal. Calcd for C9H11NO2: C,
65.44; H, 6.71; N, 8.48. Found: C, 65.50; H, 6.73; N, 8.44.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 75% ee
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric reduction of α-keto aldoxime O-ethers
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bosiak, Mariusz J.; Pakulski, Marcin M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2011), (2), 316-324

