$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Table 1. Synthesis of 2,3,5-Trisubstituted Pyrroles 4a Under nitrogen
atmosphere, a magnetic stirring bar, KOBut (22.4 mg, 0.2 mmol), 1 (3.75
mg, 0.005 mmol), propiophenone (0.53 mL, 4.0 mmol) and L-valinol (0.22
mL, 2.0 mmol) were added at room temperature to a vessel equipped with a
Young’s stopcock (75 mL). The reaction system was closed and heated at
165 °C for 24 h under stirring. The mixture was cooled down to room
temperature and a minimum amount of saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution was
added to quench the reaction. The crude mixture was diluted with CDCl3
and also analyzed by 1H NMR using 1,1,1,2-tetrachloroethane as internal
standard. After 1H NMR measurement, the crude mixture was diluted with
CH2Cl2 and washed with water. The aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2
(× 3) and the combined organic layers were dried over Na2SO4. After
filtration, solvents of the filtrate were removed under vacuum and the
resulting crude oil was purified by column chromatography on silica gel
(toluene/n-hexane = 1/2) to give the desired product
5-isopropyl-3-methyl-2-phenyl-1H-pyrrole (4aa) (257 mg, 64%).
5-isopropyl-3-methyl-2-phenyl-1H-pyrrole (4aa), yield 77%, 5a 74%. 4aa Rf
(toluene/n-hexane = 1/2): 0.34. IR (neat): 3457, 3054, 2985, 1606, 1515,
1421, 1265, 896, 740 705 cm-1. 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.26 (d, J =
6.8 Hz, 6H), 2.24 (s, 3H), 2.88 (sep, J = 6.9 Hz, 1H), 5.85 (d, J = 2.8
Hz, 1H), 7.15-7.18 (m, 1H), 7.33-7.37 (m, 4H), 7.75 (br, 1H). 13C NMR
(150 MHz, CDCl3): δ 12.6, 22.6, 27.1, 107.3, 116.0, 125.4, 126.0, 126.4,
128.6, 134.0, 138.7. HRMS (FAB): m/z calcd for [C14H17N+] ([M+]):
199.1361, found: 199.1369.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimized on catalyst: base ratio and catalyst used, no solvent,
optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM The Dual Role of Ruthenium and Alkali Base Catalysts in Enabling a
Conceptually New Shortcut to N-Unsubstituted Pyrroles through Unmasked
α-Amino Aldehydes
