$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Table 1. Synthesis of 2,3,5-Trisubstituted
Pyrroles 4a Under nitrogen atmosphere, a magnetic stirring bar, KOBut
(22.4 mg, 0.2 mmol), 1 (3.75 mg, 0.005 mmol), propiophenone (0.53 mL, 4.0
mmol) and L-valinol (0.22 mL, 2.0 mmol) were added at room temperature to
a vessel equipped with a Young’s stopcock (75 mL). The reaction system
was closed and heated at 165 °C for 24 h under stirring. The mixture was
cooled down to room temperature and a minimum amount of saturated aqueous
NH4Cl solution was added to quench the reaction. The crude mixture was
diluted with CDCl3 and also analyzed by 1H NMR using
1,1,1,2-tetrachloroethane as internal standard. After 1H NMR measurement,
the crude mixture was diluted with CH2Cl2 and washed with water. The
aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2 (× 3) and the combined organic
layers were dried over Na2SO4. After filtration, solvents of the filtrate
were removed under vacuum and the resulting crude oil was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel (toluene/n-hexane = 1/2) to give the
desired product 5-isopropyl-3-methyl-2-phenyl-1H-pyrrole (4aa) (257 mg,
64%). Table 1. Synthesis of 2,3,5-Trisubstituted Pyrroles 4a
5-isopropyl-2-(4-methoxyphenyl)-3-methyl-1H-pyrrole (4ac) 4ac 59%, 5c
67%. 4ac:Rf (toluene/n-hexane = 1/2): 0.26. IR (neat): 3393, 2959, 2868,
1523, 1460, 1245, 1177, 1038, 831, 796 cm-1. 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3): δ
1.27 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 6H), 2.20 (s, 3H), 2.91 (sep, J = 6.9 Hz, 1H), 3.81
(s, 3H), 5.83 (d, J = 2.8 Hz, 1H), 6.91-6.92 (m, 2H), 7.30-7.32 (m, 2H),
7.73 (br, 1H). 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3): δ 12.3, 22.7, 27.1, 55.3, 106.9,
114.1, 114.8, 126.4, 126.8, 127.5, 138.1, 157.7. HRMS (FAB): m/z calcd
for [C15H19NO+] ([M+]): 229.1467, found: 229.1477.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM The Dual Role of Ruthenium and Alkali Base Catalysts in Enabling a
Conceptually New Shortcut to N-Unsubstituted Pyrroles through Unmasked
α-Amino Aldehydes
